<title>Relay Switch Circuit</title>
supply "12 V"                  the + rail and 0 V (GND); battery B1 "9 V" draws a battery
pin P1 "Arduino D7"            a microcontroller pin (5 V; write 3.3V for an ESP32 or a Pi); its board's GND is joined to 0 V
led D1 P1 red                  an LED lit by pin P1 (led D1 alone: from + to 0 V). Lantern adds and sizes its resistor
relay K1 "12 V coil"           a relay coil; also lamp L1, motor M1, buzzer BZ1, solenoid Y1
transistor Q1 K1 P1            an NPN transistor switching K1, its base driven by P1 -- Lantern adds the base resistor, and the
                               diode across a relay, motor or solenoid. A pin naming a relay or motor gets a transistor added.
switch S1 P2                   a push button read by pin P2 (Lantern adds the pull-down; write pullup for a pull-up)
sensor LDR1 P3                 a light sensor read by P3, with its divider resistor (thermistor TH1 P3; pot RV1 P3)
resistor R1 "330 ohm" D1       a resistor you size yourself, in series with D1 (Lantern checks the current)
capacitor C1 "100 uF"          across the supply, its + to the + rail
note <text>                    a line of text under the drawing
END

MAKE CODE:
void setup() {
  pinMode(P1, OUTPUT);
  pinMode(P2, INPUT_PULLUP);
  pinMode(P3, INPUT);
  digitalWrite(P1, HIGH);
}

void loop() {
  if (digitalRead(P2) == LOW) {
    digitalWrite(P1, LOW);
  } else {
    digitalWrite(P1, HIGH);
  }
}

